course: dictionary
lesson: 15516
title: Subside: calming down or going lower
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When something subsides, it gets calmer, weaker or lower. You can think of it as going down or calming down. «The storm began to subside after midnight.» The storm did not stop at once. It got weaker, and the wind dropped.
explain: Subside has three main meanings. Storms, pain and strong feelings can subside, becoming less strong. Water can subside, sinking to a lower level. Land or buildings can subside, sinking slowly into the ground. Ask yourself: is it getting calmer, lower, or sinking?
explain: Try the swap test. Put a plain word into the sentence, such as die down or go down. «The flood waters subsided» becomes «The flood waters went down», and it still makes sense, so subside means go down here.
fact: Subside is a verb: subside, subsides, subsided, subsiding.
fact: The noun is subsidence, which means sinking into the ground.
fact: «Subsided» means became calmer, weaker or lower.
fact: Plain words for subside are die down, calm down, go down and sink.
fact: Subside is a formal word, often found in news and science writing.
exercise: «The wind began to subside by the evening.» What does subside mean here? | Blew the roof away | Grew stronger and louder | Turned into snow | *Became calmer and weaker
exercise: «The flood waters subsided, and the road was dry again.» What happened to the water? | It froze solid | It turned into steam | It grew deeper and wider | *It went down to a lower level
exercise: «The old house began to subside into the soft ground.» What is happening to the house? | *It is sinking lower into the ground | It is being painted | It is growing taller | It is floating away
test: «After the medicine, Sam's fever slowly subsided.» What does subsided mean? | Turned into a song | Went on a holiday | Became much hotter | *Became lower and weaker
test: Which plain word could replace subside in «The noise will subside soon»? | Grow | *Die down | Bounce | Explode
exam: Jayden says subside is a fancy word. Why is it useful to know? | It means exactly the same as jump | It is only used in fairy tales | *It appears in news and science, and can mean calmer, lower or sinking | It is the name of a river
